          %h3#group_of_hamiltonian_symplectomorphisms Group of Hamiltonian symplectomorphisms
          %p
            The auto-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectomorphisms"} symplectomorphisms
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic manifold
            form a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+vector+fields"} symplectic vector fields
            generate the connected component. The Hamiltonian vector fields among the symplectic ones generate the group of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+symplectomorphisms"} Hamiltonian symplectomorphisms
          %p (…)
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian"}> Hamiltonian
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+action"} Hamiltonian action
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+symplectomorphism"} Hamiltonian symplectomorphism
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reeb+vector+field"} Reeb vector field
            %li
              %p
                The Hamiltonian vector field of a given function may also be called its
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+gradient"} symplectic gradient
            %li
              %p
                The generalization to
                = succeed "/" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multisymplectic+geometry"} multisymplectic geometry
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-plectic+geometry"} n-plectic geometry
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+n-vector+fields"} Hamiltonian n-vector fields
          %h2#references References
          %p
            Named after
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Rowan+Hamilton"} William Rowan Hamilton
          %p A textbook reference is section II.3 in
          %ul#Brylinski
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Luc+Brylinski"}> Jean-Luc Brylinski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Loop spaces, characteristic classes and geometric quantization
          %p
            For more references on the ordinary notion of Hamiltonian vector fields see the references at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+geometry"} symplectic geometry
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
          %p
            The notion of Hamiltonian vector field in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-plectic+geometry"} n-plectic geometry
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"}> Chris Rogers
              ,
              %em Higher symplectic geometry
              PhD thesis (2011) (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1106.4068"}> arXiv:1106.4068
              )
          %p
            The notion of Hamiltonian vector field for
            = succeed "-plectic" do
